Algorithm 1: scContam audit pipeline

Input: Benchmark $\mathcal{B}$ , reference subsample $\mathcal{R}$ , scFM $\theta$ , donor and cell-type metadata.

Output: Per-cell { $J^{*} (c), p_{c}$ }; donor-matched gap statistics and permutation $p$ .

Step 1 (Signal A): Compute MinHash sketch ($m=128$ ) for each $c\in\mathcal{B}\cup\mathcal{R}$ ;

for $c\in\mathcal{B}$ do

Compute $J^{*} (c)$ via banded LSH ($b=16, r=8$ ) on $\mathcal{R}$ ;

Draw 1000 permutation sketches; compute $p_{c}$ from Eq. 4;

end

Step 2 (Embedding): Extract $\theta$ -embedding $\mathbf{e}_{c}$ for all $c\in\mathcal{B}$ ;

Step 3 (Donor-matched gap):;

for each $(t,d)$ pair with $n_{clean},n_{contam}\geq n_{\min}$ do

Compute $\Delta_{(t,d),\theta}$ via Eq. 8;

end

Step 4 (Permutation null): Shuffle contamination labels within each $(t,d)$ group,

repeat Step 3, $B=500$ trials;

Step 5 (Negative control, optional): Repeat Steps 3-4 on a Signal-A-clean dataset

with random pseudo-contamination;
